=========================================================================================================
19_gnn_strong_baselines.py — Stronger neural baselines on the shared outer folds
=========================================================================================================

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  The graph network of steps 09 and 12 was trained from scratch, one network per fold. A fair
  objection is that a         stronger neural model might have matched the classical ensembles.
  This step tries four: an average of five graph         networks, a graph network that also
  receives the RDKit descriptors, a graph network that starts from CheMeleon (a         model
  pretrained on about a million PubChem molecules), and a plain neural network on the Morgan
  fingerprints. All         are scored on the same 25 folds as every other model and compared with
  the same corrected tests.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  100 variant x fold tasks to run (0 already in the checkpoint)
  12 workers x 4 threads
